---
import RngChordsApp from "../app/RngChordsApp";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/app.css";
import "../styles/table.css";

const pageTitle = "RNG Chords | Random Chord Generator";
const pageDescription =
	"Roll dice to get a chord progression. Keep the chords you like, reroll the rest, and download the result as a MIDI file. Free, no account.";
const pageUrl = Astro.site
	? new URL("/", Astro.site).toString()
	: "https://rngchords.jonathanrreed.com/";
const socialImage = Astro.site
	? new URL("/social-card.svg", Astro.site).toString()
	: "/social-card.svg";
const authorSameAs = [
	"https://jonathanrreed.com/",
	"https://github.com/JonathanRReed",
];
const publishedDate = "2026-04-21";
const modifiedDate = "2026-10-21";
const author = {
	"@type": "Person",
	name: "Jonathan R. Reed",
	url: "https://jonathanrreed.com",
	sameAs: authorSameAs,
};

// Site-level JSON-LD describes the public tool without inventing independent
// ratings or reviews that do not exist.
const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "WebSite",
	"@id": `${pageUrl}#website`,
	name: "RNG Chords",
	description: pageDescription,
	url: pageUrl,
	image: socialImage,
	isAccessibleForFree: true,
	inLanguage: "en-US",
	datePublished: publishedDate,
	dateModified: modifiedDate,
	author,
	creator: author,
};

// Project-level JSON-LD. The tool has no independent ratings or reviews, so it
// deliberately avoids the SoftwareApplication rich-result type.
const creativeWorkData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "CreativeWork",
	"@id": `${pageUrl}#project`,
	name: "RNG Chords",
	description: pageDescription,
	url: pageUrl,
	image: socialImage,
	isAccessibleForFree: true,
	inLanguage: "en-US",
	datePublished: publishedDate,
	dateModified: modifiedDate,
	isPartOf: { "@id": `${pageUrl}#website` },
	keywords: "random chord generator, chord progression generator, dice, MIDI export",
	author,
	creator: author,
};
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} path="/" jsonLd={[structuredData, creativeWorkData]} author>
	<RngChordsApp client:load />

	<section class="guide" aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
		<h2 id="how-it-works">How the chords are picked</h2>

		<p>
			In Easy mode each die becomes one chord, and its size (d4 up to d20) sets
			how far that chord can wander. Advanced mode uses five dice, one each for
			the root, quality, extensions, inversion, and rhythm. Manual mode skips
			the dice: type something like <code>Cmaj9, Am11, D7b9, G13</code> or build
			a chord from parts.
		</p>
		<p>
			The dice total picks the key from nine centers: C, G, D, A, E, F,
			B&#9837;, E&#9837;, and A&#9837;. Every root comes from that key's major
			scale and the quality is rolled separately, so a minor chord can land where
			a major one "should" be.
		</p>

		<h3>Chord style</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Simple</strong> uses major, minor, and dominant chords with at
				most a 6, 7, or maj7 on top.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Color</strong> adds sus4, diminished, and augmented chords, plus
				9ths, 11ths, 13ths, and altered notes.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Tension</strong> gives every chord an extension, allows deeper
				inversions, and lets a chord shrink to an eighth note.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Everything runs in your browser, and your last idea is saved in local
			storage. More background is on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<SiteFooter />
</Base>
